  Snippet:
  ```ts
  if (
    service?.type !== "AtprotoPersonalDataServer" &&
    service?.id !== "#atproto_pds"
  ) {
    continue;
  }
  ```
  This accepts a service when either its type or ID matches, so an unrelated endpoint can be selected as the PDS. Reject when either field is wrong:
  ```ts
  if (
    service?.type !== "AtprotoPersonalDataServer" ||
    service?.id !== "#atproto_pds"
  ) continue;
  ```

- `src/utils/standard-site-reader.server.ts:106-112` — severity 3/5, confidence 0.99  
  Snippet:
  ```ts
  const text = await response.text();
  if (text.length > MAX_RECORD_BYTES) {
    throw new Error("Record response exceeded the size limit.");
  }
  ```
  `text.length` measures UTF-16 code units, not response bytes, so multibyte UTF-8 records can exceed the stated byte limit when `Content-Length` is absent or inaccurate. Measure encoded byte length with `TextEncoder`, or enforce the limit while reading the response stream.

- `src/utils/standard-site.ts:301-326` — severity 3/5, confidence 0.96  
  Snippet:
  ```ts
  if (
    !documentParts ||
    !publicationParts ||
    documentParts.did !== publicationParts.did
  ) {
    return null;
  }
  ...
  viewerUrl: standardSiteDocumentUrl(
    documentParts.did,
    publicationParts.rkey,
    documentParts.rkey,
  ),
  ```
  `DocumentRef` stores `publicationUri`, but reconstruction only compares repository DIDs. If the cached publication changes to another publication under the same DID, the old document rkey is incorrectly combined with the new publication rkey. Validate `doc.publicationUri === publication.uri` when loading, with an explicit legacy fallback or migration if older entries lack that field.

